-- title:
--   Process all sketch states of one predecessor graph vertex
-- statement:
--   Fix valid layer and sketch indices $i,a$, a target vertex $v$ and predecessor vertex $u$. Suppose the core native invariant identifies the previous matrix with semantic layer $p\le k$, and the accumulator equals the predecessor prefix $P(u,0)$: the sum of weighted incoming contributions from vertices below $u$. With the previous-state counter empty, the predecessor-vertex procedure advances $u$ and establishes
--   $$
--   \operatorname{Acc}'=P(u+1,0).
--   $$
--   The added term is zero if $(u,v)$ is absent; otherwise it is the sum over all $k$ previous states, weighted by their shared decoded later-sketch signs. All other state is restored. With $W=100(1+n+k)^2$, trial-bit count $T$ and $m$ stored arcs, the bound is
--   $$
--   (C_{\rm cell}(nk,T,k,W)+56)k+7000(n+1)(m+1)+15000(W+1)^2+1000(k+1).
--   $$
--   This is the arc-conditioned predecessor step in the graph recurrence.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/PredecessorVertex.lean, line 22; source snapshot SHA-256 a8f6c501e7d7896db1f49a02d30ea7fdf84141e389a50a4c0594613cc75c7dce.

